From 7bbd6de783a4674e253a3ea8a9e605b36633b907 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:13:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 118/120] render: a puppet's effects run on its image, its
 material draws the mesh last
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A puppet layer with effects drew its mesh first (the material pass, posed, into the layer FBO) and ran
the effects on that posed picture. WE runs them on the image itself — in texture space, as for a plain
image — and the material (genericimage4, the only pass that skins) draws the mesh last from their
output. Measured on 3013489778's girl (puppet layer 161, a time `pulse` with an opacity mask painted
for another layer): with the mask swapped for a ramp in u, then in v (private copies, WE under Proton),
the value each pixel of the posed girl samples is its part's place in the 4380 x 2998 atlas — the face
u 0.31-0.40, v 0.61-0.70, constant per part, jumping between hair strands. Ours sampled the posed
layer's smooth position (face u 0.52-0.61), which fell between the mask's blobs: WE's girl pulses,
ours barely did.

With effects (and only effects) after the material, the material pass moves to the end of the chain:
the first effect copies the image into the FBO (normal blending, as the material does in front of a
plain image's effects), the effects run there, and the material draws the mesh into the scene reading
the chain's output as g_Texture0 (CPass::setInputIsTexture0 overrides the material's own texture) at
the mesh's coordinates on the composite (the texture's over its copy limits). Its blending stays its
own (translucent where it was normal). A puppet without effects, or with a tint / colour-blend / fog
pass after them, keeps the old order.

After: the ramp maps match WE's (face row u 0.315-0.406 vs WE 0.314-0.402). 3013489778 against WE:
0.125 -> 0.003. Host test puppet_effects_run_on_its_image (red 131 unpatched, 26 patched).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/reports/scene-we-ref.md 3013489778 (the girl doesn't pulse)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vg3T4kWN88ooeafgoHLbfM
